Discover and follow relevant internal links from these pages. Crawl linked official FAQs, downloadable PDFs, user guides, service descriptions, forms, checklists, regulations, announcements, and other documents relevant to pre-incorporation and post-incorporation services.
Prioritise official primary sources. Where necessary, consult legislation such as the Companies and Allied Matters Act 2020 (CAMA), applicable regulations, and other relevant Nigerian laws through authoritative government sources.
Research requirements
•	Extract factual requirements, procedures, eligibility criteria, required documents, filing routes, fees, applicable deadlines, exceptions, and service timelines.
•	Identify the source URL and retrieval date for every substantive regulatory claim.
•	Extract relevant text from PDFs and inspect scanned documents using OCR where necessary.
•	Distinguish between current procedures on the new i-CRP and any obsolete procedures described in older documents.
•	Verify whether each procedure is current before publishing it.
•	Identify inconsistencies between older CAC publications and newer official portal guidance.
•	Prioritise the latest applicable official guidance, legislation, and formal notices. Do not assume that the newest webpage automatically overrides legislation.
•	Never invent filing requirements, statutory fees, penalties, deadlines, approval guarantees, or required documents.
•	If information cannot be verified, label it “Verification required” and send it for editorial review rather than presenting it as established fact.
•	Respect website access restrictions, robots.txt, rate limits, copyright, and applicable terms of use. Do not bypass authentication or access controls.
•	Do not copy the entire CAC website or reproduce long copyrighted passages. Summarise and explain official information in original, accessible language.
•	Do not reproduce personal data found in publicly accessible corporate records.
Deliver a research inventory containing source URL, page or document title, publication or update date where available, retrieval date, topics covered, relevant extracted facts, and verification status.
